  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Request (pt-BR)**: \"Melhore esse jogo com ost, gr\303\241ficos e sprites principalmente o fundo do jogo.\" (Improve the attached Super Pang World Tour HTML game with OST, graphics, and sprites \342\200\224 especially the game backgrounds.)\n- **Source Material**: Attached single-file HTML game `/public/assets/aistudio/super_pang_world_tour_remastered__1__a6880c5c.html` (provided inline in full). Contains 24 stages (world landmarks + Moon & Mars), aviator hero, 4 bubble sizes, 6 power-ups (Double Harpoon, Sticky Cable, Shield, Clock Freeze, Dynamite, Extra Life), destructible/indestructible blocks, and world/space map travel cutscenes.\n- **Success Criteria**:\n  1. Massively upgraded **24 scenic game backgrounds** with painterly layered art, offscreen static layer caching, live animated midground/weather/water reflections, and theme-matched arena floors.\n  2. Massively upgraded **OST & SFX** (Web Audio lookahead scheduler with zero jitter, master dynamics compressor + subtle delay, full 64-step / 4-bar compositions across all 24 destinations + title + map travel themes with distinct regional instrument timbres, chords/arpeggios, basslines, and drums).\n  3. Massively upgraded **sprites & game feel** (detailed aviator sprite with physics scarf, gleaming goggles, muzzle flash, recoil, automatic spacesuit + glass helmet on Moon & Mars, iridescent arcade bubbles with squash-and-stretch & ice shell, braided harpoon cables with grappling claws, theme-matched beveled blocks, rotating power-up medallions, combo multiplier, and tactile hitstop).\n  4. Full-viewport React/Vite Game Shell (`Title Screen` with live-world rotating scenic backdrop & bespoke SVG title emblem -> `Playing` -> `Pause` / `Stage Clear` / `Map Travel` / `Game Over` / `Victory`), clean Portuguese UI, zero-pill discipline, low-occlusion HUD.\n  5. Clean compilation & lint pass (`compile_applet` + `lint_applet`).\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Skills Read\n- `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md` (read in full)\n- `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/4_games_2d_casual.md` (read in full)\n\n### Completed Files (all newly written / updated)\n- `/metadata.json` \342\200\224 Named `\"Super Pang World Tour\"` with pt-BR description.\n- `/index.html` \342\200\224 Updated `<title>`, meta/OG tags, and loaded Google Fonts (`Chakra Petch`, `Press Start 2P`).\n- `/src/index.css` \342\200\224 Tailwind CSS v4 setup, `.font-arcade`, `.font-ui`, `.tabular-nums`, modal pop animation, custom scrollbar for stage grid.\n- `/src/game/types.ts` \342\200\224 Full TypeScript interfaces (`GameState`, `PowerupType`, `ThemeId`, `RegionGroup`, `LevelDef`, `Player`, `Bubble`, `Harpoon`, `Block`, `PowerupItem`, `Particle`, `Shard`, `ShockRing`, `ScorePopup`, `TravelState`, `HudSnapshot`).\n- `/src/game/levels.ts` \342\200\224 World/physics constants (`WORLD_W=960`, `WORLD_H=540`, `GROUND_Y=500`, `BASE_GRAVITY=880`), `BUBBLE_SPECS`, `POWERUP_DEFS`, and all 24 `LEVELS` with color palettes, swatches, regions, map coordinates, gravity scales, bubble formations, and block layouts.\n- `/src/game/audio.ts` \342\200\224 Complete `AudioEngine` class + `OST_TRACKS` catalog (24 regional 64-step 4-bar compositions + `title` + `travel`), Web Audio lookahead scheduler, dynamics compressor + slapback delay bus, 25 regional instrument profiles, chord/arp engine, regional drum kits, and punchy arcade SFX (with combo pitch climbing).\n- `/src/game/bgHelpers.ts` \342\200\224 Deterministic `mulberry32` PRNG, painterly brushes (`fillSky`, `paintHazeBand`, `paintSunWithBloom`, `paintCloudBank`, `paintSculptedMountain`, `paintFoliageCluster`, `paintArchRow`, `paintSkyscraper`, `paintBackdropFinishing`), live weather/particle pools & `updateAmbientWeather`, `drawTwinklingStars`, `drawBird`, `drawSwayingPalm`, `drawWaterShimmer`.\n- `/src/game/backgrounds.ts` \342\200\224 Offscreen-cached (`staticBackdropCache`) painterly static backdrops for all 24 destinations, real-time animated midground/weather layer (`drawBackground`), and theme-matched architectural floor/frame renderer (`drawArenaFrame`).\n- `/src/game/sprites.ts` \342\200\224 High-craft renderers for theme-matched blocks (`drawBlocks`, `getBlockThemeStyle`), braided harpoons (`drawHarpoons`), iridescent bubbles with hit-flash & ice shell (`drawBubbles`), aviator + automatic Moon/Mars spacesuit & glass helmet (`drawPlayer`), glowing power-up medallions (`drawPowerups`), effects (`drawEffects`), stage intro banner (`drawStageIntroBanner`), and painted World/Space map travel cutscene (`renderMapTravel`).\n- `/src/game/engine.ts` \342\200\224 Decoupled 60fps `SuperPangEngine` class managing `requestAnimationFrame` outside React, clamped `dt <= 0.05`, hitstop, combo multiplier, buffered fire input, `clearInputs()` on window blur, live-world scenic cycling showcase on Title Screen, and throttled HUD snapshots.\n- `/src/components/TitleLogo.tsx` \342\200\224 Bespoke inline `<svg>` arcade title lockup (`SUPER PANG \302\267 WORLD TOUR \302\267 24 DESTINOS`) with wings and globe crest.\n- `/src/components/HudBar.tsx` \342\200\224 Low-occlusion world-matched HUD bar (`tabular-nums`, SVG heart lives, time bar, active power-ups, Stage Select / Music / SFX Mute / Pause controls).\n- `/src/components/Overlays.tsx` \342\200\224 Title Screen overlay, 24-Stage Destination Selector with region filter tabs & per-stage OST preview button, Pause, Stage Clear, Game Over, and Final Victory modals.\n- `/src/App.tsx` \342\200\224 Full-viewport Game Shell mounting isolated `<canvas>`, keyboard + touch controls, skip map button, HUD, and overlays.\n\n### Not Yet Run\n- `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` have NOT been run yet (all files were just written in the final turn before compaction).\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Image Generation Constraint**: The attachment metadata explicitly noted `\"Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\"` Because the game has 24 distinct destinations, building an offscreen-cached painterly Canvas 2D backdrop engine with real-time animated midground/weather layers provides 100% cohesive, zero-latency, 60fps scenic art across all 24 stages without risking mismatched or broken images.\n- **No Extra Packages Needed**: All needed icons (`lucide-react`), React 19, Tailwind v4, and TypeScript are already installed in `package.json`.\n- **Stage Select Audio UX**: Added a quick OST preview button (`<Music />`) on every stage card in the 24-destination selector, plus region filter tabs (`Todos`, `\303\201sia & Pac\303\255fico`, `Am\303\251ricas`, `Europa & \303\201frica`, `Espa\303\247o`). Note: check if closing the Stage Select modal while on `START` should stop any previewed OST or let it play cleanly \342\200\224 currently `onCloseStages` simply sets `showStageSelect(false)`, which is fine, or optionally check behavior if paused.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- No errors encountered yet (build & lint have not been executed yet).\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- All source files are written and in place in `/src/...`, `/index.html`, and `/metadata.json`.\n- No background tasks or external services are running.\n\n## 6. Next Steps\n1. **Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together in parallel** in the very next turn to verify TypeScript compilation, Vite bundling, and ESLint cleanliness.\n2. **Fix any TypeScript or ESLint issues** reported by `compile_applet` / `lint_applet` (e.g., unused variables, strict type checks, missing imports) and re-run both tools until both pass cleanly (max 3 fix attempts).\n3. **Quickly sanity-check edge cases if touching code**:\n   - Ensure `Overlays.tsx` when closing `showStageSelect` from `PAUSED` or `START` behaves intuitively (in `App.tsx`, opening stages calls `engineRef.current?.pauseForModal()`, which puts `PLAYING` into `PAUSED`; closing stage select leaves it in `PAUSED` so user sees the Pause modal and can click `CONTINUAR`, or `START` if opened from title).\n4. **Respond concisely in Portuguese (pt-BR)** \342\200\224 2\342\200\2233 plain-language sentences summarizing the improvements (24 cen\303\241rios ilustrados e animados com cache, nova trilha sonora regional em 4 compassos e sprites/efeitos aprimorados), with no code snippets, file paths, or bulleted feature recaps.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Language**: Respond in Brazilian Portuguese (matching the user\'s prompt).\n- **Concise Final Response**: 2\342\200\2233 simple, plain-language sentences max. Omit code snippets, implementation details, bulleted feature recaps, build/test logs, hype, and file paths.\n- **Verification**: Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together on the final check.\n- **No Unsolicited AI Features or Image Generation**: Keep purely client-side 2D arcade game with Web Audio + Canvas 2D; do not add chatbots or call `generate_image`.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 23
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
    total_subagent_count: 0
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport fs from \'fs\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [\n      react(),\n      tailwindcss(),\n      // Copies src/assets into dist/ so root-relative URLs like\n      // \"/src/assets/images/...\" (e.g. generate_image output) still resolve\n      // in production builds. Do not remove.\n      {\n        name: \'copy-unbundled-src-assets\',\n        apply: \'build\',\n        closeBundle(error?: Error): void {\n          if (error) {\n            return;\n          }\n          const distDir = path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\');\n          const srcAssets = path.resolve(__dirname, \'src/assets\');\n          const distAssets = path.resolve(distDir, \'src/assets\');\n          if (fs.existsSync(distDir) && fs.existsSync(srcAssets)) {\n            fs.cpSync(srcAssets, distAssets, {recursive: true, force: true});\n          }\n        },\n      },\n    ],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
